  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Earthquake Cash Plus Services</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(USAID Middle East Regional (MER)):  The Earthquake Cash Plus Services (ECAPS) activity will provide targeted and integrated education and social support services to communities affected by the September 2023 Al Haouz earthquake. .ECAPS complements the Government of Morocco&apos;s emergency cash transfer program by piloting wrap-around education and social support services for affected children and families. In the process, ECAPS is building the capacity of local partners, strengthening community feedback mechanisms, and generating evidence to inform sustainability at scale..ECAPS will facilitate uninterrupted access to education through light rehabilitation of damaged schools and the installation of temporary classrooms. ECAPS intends to improve student learning outcomes through remedial classes and extracurricular activities (e.g. summer camps and student clubs). Additionally, ECAPS will work with the Ministry of Education, Mohammed V University, and a core group of psychologists and social workers to develop and deliver psychosocial support training in three affected provinces (Al Haouz, Chichaoua, and Taroudant). In the process, ECAPS is supporting a long-term model for psychosocial support and emergency preparedness in the public education system. ....The full $900,000 of funding in this activity will attribute to the BED - Girls in Conflict earmark...</narrative>
  </description>
